# .Renviron.example
# Copy this to .Renviron and fill in the values you need. .Renviron is
# gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# The app runs with NONE of these set: it falls back to the sibling checkout at
# ../fwise-data/ and writes submissions to ../fwise-data/inbox/.

# ---- The data repository -----------------------------------------------------
# THE ONE VARIABLE A DEPLOYMENT NEEDS, and the only secret in the project.
#
# fwise-data is private, so an unauthenticated raw.githubusercontent.com URL
# returns 404. Set this to a fine-grained GitHub PAT - resource owner
# freshwaterLife, scoped to fwise-data, Contents: Read and write - and the app
# reads the data and writes submissions over the GitHub API.
#
# Leave it unset locally. The app then reads ../fwise-data/ and writes
# submissions to ../fwise-data/inbox/, making no network calls at all.
#
# The repository and branch are constants in R/config.R, not variables. Neither
# is a secret and neither varies.
# FWISE_DATA_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# ---- Override, not normally needed -------------------------------------------
# Wins over the token. Use it to point a test deploy at a fork, a branch or a
# local path without a code change:
#
#   /some/path   read that directory
#   https://...  read that base URL over plain HTTPS with NO credential. Cannot
#                write, so submissions will fail.
#
# Point it at the directory holding metadata.json and schema/, NOT at schema/
# itself. A trailing slash is tolerated.
#
# Setting it explicitly, as below, means the app still finds the data when run
# from a different working directory.
# FWISE_DATA_SOURCE=/absolute/path/to/fwise-data

# ---- Submissions -------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing further to configure. FWISE_DATA_TOKEN above covers both directions:
# submissions are committed to inbox/ in the same repository the data is read
# from. Without a token they are written to ../fwise-data/inbox/ instead, in the
# same one-file-per-submission shape, so the QA loop is identical.
